# broiler-shared-package pin 1
#
# One package of the committed, hash-pinned feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c); milestone SJL-2.7): a shared
# JavaScript library package whose home is the Broiler.JS repository, retained here byte for byte so
# that a restore needs no other repository's folder and no network for it. NuGet.config's package
# source mapping sends the Broiler.ECMAScript prefix to this directory and to nuget.org; the lock
# file of a project that references it records `content-hash`, and rule I1 holds that hash to this
# pin and to the allow-list.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. Packed on 2026-10-17 in the Broiler.JS repository, from `upstream-commit`, in a
# clean checkout of it, with `dotnet pack Broiler.ECMAScript/Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation -c Release
# -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true`; Broiler.ECMAScript/Directory.Build.props sets the version,
# 0.1.0-preview.5, at that commit. The nuspec's repository element records the same commit, which
# rule I7 reads. `content-hash` is NuGet's: the base64 SHA-512 of the .nupkg's bytes, which is what a
# lock file records. `sha256` is over the same bytes. It is not on nuget.org: the pin is taken again
# from the published package when it is published, as Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms' pins were.
#
# WHAT IT IS. The time data home's generator (milestone SJL-8.2; Broiler.VM's JSD-0076), namespace
# Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation.Time: the tz, CLDR time zone key and calendar pin readers, the tz
# compiler, the time zone and calendar table generators and the source writers, ported from this
# repository's architecture tests, with no dependency. It carries no table and no pin file: its
# caller hands it the pins' text and the archives' bytes. Admitted TEST-ONLY for
# Broiler.VM.Architecture.Tests at SJL-8.5: rules N29 to N32 regenerate the time zone and calendar
# tables with it from this repository's pins, and rule I4 holds the data versions it declares to those
# pins (decision SJL-D-6 (c): "the generator reaches each engine's tests as a pinned, test-only
# package, and never a product closure"). No release may ship it (eng/verify-feed.ps1). Its
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md is the Broiler.JS repository's, which names it as code ported from this
# repository and says it carries no data.

id Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation
version 0.1.0-preview.5
file Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation.0.1.0-preview.5.nupkg
content-hash fb0sV5AeISGfIw1auTKb/4S5t3YlU01Ibrj4fxRsVZ2r/jsjz9bqnuUuAAqvbK5re4hdJE/95qaugn2TNhLrqg==
sha256 8931b443b5da319de1921ebd65af0c89f479d3f504113e237b64b6a9a60884d6
upstream Broiler-Platform/broiler.js
upstream-commit 2d37a38a2560b076ebf2ca29989bfe20db64ed64
